From 15e84f2604106d07696f510d5bfc6479565ee913 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kartatz <105828205+Kartatz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 21:14:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ld: Add --pack-dyn-relocs=android[+relr] support

Add a new --pack-dyn-relocs=STYLE option that stores the dynamic
relocations of an ELF output file in the Android packed relocation
format (APS2 -- SHT_ANDROID_REL/SHT_ANDROID_RELA sections with
DT_ANDROID_REL{A,SZ} dynamic tags), understood by Android's dynamic
linker.  Supported styles are:

  none       plain .rel.dyn/.rela.dyn (default).
  relr       equivalent to -z pack-relative-relocs.
  android    pack all .rel.dyn/.rela.dyn relocations in APS2.
  android+relr  additionally divert R_*_RELATIVE relocations to a
              .relr.dyn section on targets that support it, leaving
              only the rest (e.g. GLOB_DAT, IRELATIVE) in APS2.

PLT relocations referenced by DT_JMPREL are always left in plain
format.  When the packed section ends up empty (all relocations
diverted to .relr.dyn), the DT_ANDROID_* entries are removed instead
of pointing at an invalid blob, matching what the bionic loader
expects.

The encoder follows the same APS2 layout as bionic and LLD: the
.rela.dyn section keeps its allocated size so other section file
offsets are unaffected, then at final-link the blob is written over
the plain relocations (zero-padded) and this_hdr.sh_size is shrunk
to the blob size.  Output binaries have been verified to decode
identically to plain links with both a custom Python decoder and
llvm-readelf (LLD's decoder), on x86_64-linux, x86_64-android,
i386-linux and aarch64-android, including the bundled-android
android-gcc-cross toolchain and an NDK-clang cross build of Nouzen
(curl+nghttp2+bearssl+zstd+libarchive+...) targeting x86_64-android
(216 vs 180 dynamic relocations per compiler, both decodable).

The full ld and binutils testsuites continue to pass (3311 ld, 351
binutils cases on x86_64, plus the four new pack-dyn-relocs tests on
x86_64 and aarch64 cross builds).

include/
	* bfdlink.h (struct bfd_link_info) <pack_dyn_relocs_android>: New.
	* elf/common.h (DT_ANDROID_REL, DT_ANDROID_RELSZ, DT_ANDROID_RELA,
	DT_ANDROID_RELASZ): New dynamic tags.
	(RELOCATION_GROUPED_BY_INFO_FLAG,
	RELOCATION_GROUPED_BY_OFFSET_DELTA_FLAG,
	RELOCATION_GROUPED_BY_ADDEND_FLAG,
	RELOCATION_GROUP_HAS_ADDEND_FLAG): New.

bfd/
	* elf-bfd.h (struct elf_link_hash_table) <android_rela_sec>,
	<android_rela_contents>: New fields.
	* elf.c (assign_section_numbers) [SHT_ANDROID_REL/A]: Fix up
	sh_link to .dynsym when unset.
	(_bfd_elf_copy_private_section_data): Preserve SHT_ANDROID_REL/A
	across objcopy and relocatable link.
	* elflink.c (_bfd_elf_add_dynamic_entry): Treat DT_ANDROID_RELA and
	DT_ANDROID_REL as marking dynamic_relocs.
	(elf_android_sleb128, elf_android_reloc, elf_android_reloc_cmp,
	elf_android_encode_relocs, elf_link_android_pack_relocs): New.
	(_bfd_elf_add_dynamic_tags): Emit DT_ANDROID_REL{A,SZ} instead of
	DT_REL{A,SZ,[A]ENT} when pack_dyn_relocs_android is set.
	(_bfd_elf_final_link): Retype the unique .rel.dyn/.rela.dyn section
	to SHT_ANDROID_REL(A) and pack its relocations into APS2; remove
	empty-section DT_ANDROID_* entries; write the blob after dynobj.

binutils/
	* readelf.c (get_dynamic_type) <DT_ANDROID_REL>, <DT_ANDROID_RELSZ>,
	<DT_ANDROID_RELA>, <DT_ANDROID_RELASZ>: Print readable names.

ld/
	* ld.texi, ldlex.h, lexsup.c, emultempl/elf.em, NEWS: Plumb the
	--pack-dyn-relocs option through.
	* testsuite/ld-elf/pack-dyn-relocs{.d,-relr.d,.exp,.s,-1.c,
	-check.py}: New tests.
